<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46195" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭb-urbānus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>situated near the city of Rome</i>, <i>suburban.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rus suburbanum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rosc. Am. 46, 133</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fundus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Q. Fr. 3, 1, 3, § 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Div. 2, 32, 69</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gymnasium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					de Or. 1, 21, 98</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regio Italiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					11, 2, 61</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Italia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					26, 4, 9, § 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caulis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 4, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">peregrinatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					3, 47</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crimina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 13, 43</span></i>
			 et saep. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Substt.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭburbā-num</span></b> , i,
			n. (sc. praedium), <i>an estate near
			Rome</i>, <i>a suburban villa</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">malo esse in Tusculano aut uspiam in suburbano,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 16, 13, 6, §
				1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suburbana amicorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Verr. 2, 1, 20, § 54</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Rab. Post. 10, 26</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Q. Fr. 3, 1, 7, § 23 sq.</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id.
				Att. 12, 34, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">16, 13</span></i>, b, 1; <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 40,
				61, § 144</span></i>; <i><span class="en">31, 3, 25, §
			42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Ner. 48</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 5, 35, 3 al.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Lev.
				25, 34</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭburbāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of the towns near Rome</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 6,
			58</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
